{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2158-10-03 05:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this hospital stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2158-10-03 05:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this awful stomach pain for three days. It’s in my upper belly and goes to my back. I can’t eat, I’ve been throwing up, and I just feel so weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2158-10-03 05:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fevers or chills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2158-10-03 05:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, low-grade fevers—around 100 to 101. And night sweats. I’m also worried my GJ tube site might be infected again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2158-10-03 05:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. We checked your blood sugar in the ER—it was very high, 764. And your labs show some acid buildup, which suggests diabetic ketoacidosis, or DKA."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2158-10-03 05:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But my urine didn’t show ketones. Does that mean it’s not DKA?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2158-10-03 05:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good question. Sometimes with poor blood flow or dehydration, ketones don’t show up in urine even if DKA is starting. Your blood work still shows signs of it, so we’re treating it just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2158-10-03 05:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So what happens now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2158-10-03 05:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you IV fluids and insulin to bring your sugar down safely. We’ll also keep an eye on your electrolytes and pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2158-10-03 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar has come down to 433 after the first insulin dose. That’s improving. We’ll keep adjusting the insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2158-10-03 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it because I haven’t been eating? I haven’t taken my insulin either—I just didn’t feel like it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2158-10-03 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Not eating and skipping insulin can throw your sugars way off, even without infection. We’ll work with the diabetes team to adjust your plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2158-10-03 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My port hurts when they try to flush it. It’s been burning for weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2158-10-03 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’ll order an X-ray to check if there’s a kink or blockage. That could explain the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2158-10-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray shows a possible kink in the catheter near your collarbone. We’re going to do a port study to check the flow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2158-10-04 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2158-10-04 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You might feel some pressure, but we’ll go slow. The radiologist will explain everything before starting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2158-10-05 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The port study didn’t show a leak, but you had severe pain during the flush. The X-ray suggests pinch-off syndrome—where the catheter gets compressed between bones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2158-10-05 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why it hurts? What can we do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2158-10-05 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We recommend removing the old port and putting in a new one on the other side. A double-lumen port will give us better access."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2158-10-05 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be asleep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2158-10-05 16:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s done under general anesthesia. The surgery team will take care of you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2158-10-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar is still high this morning—403. We’re increasing your insulin dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2158-10-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel shaky sometimes. Is that the insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2158-10-06 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’re watching closely. Your levels are coming down steadily, which is good. We’ll keep adjusting to avoid lows."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2158-10-06 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My magnesium was low yesterday. Did you fix that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2158-10-06 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we gave you supplements. Your latest level is better, but still a bit low. We’ll keep giving it through the IV for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2158-10-07 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your anion gap has closed, and your bicarbonate is normal. That means the DKA is resolving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2158-10-07 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m out of the woods?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2158-10-07 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that part is under control. Now we’re focusing on your port surgery and making sure your pain is managed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2158-10-07 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous about the surgery tomorrow. Will I be okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2158-10-07 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The procedure is routine. You’ll be asleep, and the team does this often. The old port is causing pain, so replacing it should help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2158-10-08 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from surgery. The procedure went perfectly. We removed the old port from your right side and placed a new double-lumen one in your left neck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2158-10-08 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It hurts a little, but not like before. Is it safe to use already?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2158-10-08 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, both chambers are working. We’ll start using it for meds and labs. You should feel much better with the new one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2158-10-08 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My calcium dropped today. Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2158-10-08 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s low, but we’re giving you supplements. It’s likely related to your chronic pancreatitis and nutrition. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2158-10-09 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are looking good. Blood sugar is stable, electrolytes are improving, and you’re tolerating food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2158-10-09 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does that mean I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2158-10-09 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow. We want to make sure your pain is controlled and you’re comfortable with your insulin again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2158-10-09 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m supposed to get my pain meds renewed soon. Will you give me a new prescription?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2158-10-09 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on your regular pain meds here, but we won’t give a new prescription. Your contract is with your PCP, and they’ll handle the renewal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2158-10-09 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been using my albuterol more. I feel a little short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2158-10-09 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your oxygen levels are normal, and lungs are clear. It might be from anxiety or pain. Keep using your inhaler as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2158-10-09 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need to change my insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2158-10-09 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The diabetes team adjusted your sliding scale. We’ll give you a sheet to take home with the new instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I feel better, but I was worried about the port."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The new port is working well. Just keep the site clean and let your doctor know if it becomes red or painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my insulin? I don’t want another DKA episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take your glargine at bedtime and use the sliding scale with meals. Eat regularly—even if you’re not hungry—and don’t skip doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue your usual hydrocodone and ibuprofen as prescribed. Your PCP will handle the refill."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the port? Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Avoid heavy lifting for a few days. Otherwise, you can use it normally. The nurse will go over care before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I was really scared this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. You did well. Just follow up with your doctors and call if your sugar goes too high or low, or if you have pain with the port."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And thank you for listening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Take care, and we’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I stop smoking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It would help your diabetes and overall health. We can give you resources if you’re ready to try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Maybe I will. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great step. Let your PCP know—they can support you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright, the discharge papers are ready. The nurse will bring them shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. Take care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2158-10-10 07:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2158-10-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Bye for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2158-10-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2158-10-10 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2158-10-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2158-10-10 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stay safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2158-10-10 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2158-10-10 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take your time getting home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2158-10-10 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2158-10-10 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. Goodbye."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2158-10-03 04:56:00",
    "admission_end": "2158-10-10 11:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for abdominal pain and found to have diabetic ketoacidosis with a blood glucose of 764 and mild anion gap metabolic acidosis. She was treated with IV insulin and fluids, which resolved the DKA. During the hospitalization, she reported pain with port access, and imaging revealed a kinked catheter consistent with pinch-off syndrome. She underwent successful removal of the dysfunctional right subclavian port and placement of a new double-lumen port in the left internal jugular vein. Her pain was managed per her care contract, and electrolyte imbalances, including low magnesium and calcium, were corrected. She stabilized clinically, tolerated oral intake, and was discharged home with updated insulin instructions, continued pain medications, and follow-up planned with her primary care provider for medication renewal and smoking cessation support.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Mechanical complication of other vascular device, implant, and graft",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Borderline personality disorder",
      "Chronic peptic ulcer of unspecified site without mention of hemorrhage or perforation, without mention of obstruction",
      "Abdominal pain, generalized",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Status of other artificial opening of gastrointestinal tract"
    ]
  }
}
